    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0338" n="328" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg328"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Briggs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-11T08:00:00+07:00">April 11, 1945—8
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>606. We understand that Dr. Sun Fo will shortly give a broadcast to the United
                    States, the chief purpose of which will be to convey <pb facs="0339" n="329"
                        xml:id="pg329"/> assurances, prior to the convening of the San Francisco
                    Conference, that there will be no civil war in China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Briggs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
